        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nCOMMERCIAL UNIT WITH OVERHEAD ACCOMMODATION ON A LARGE SITE WITH REAR ACCESS\nDerelict Terraced Property In Need of Significant Renovation And Investment. \nSite extends to approx. 0.1763 acres / 0.0713 hectares\nIn a prime location, this expended three storey traditional town property offers enormous opportunity for a mix of residential/commercial uses. \nThe property comprises a three storey building with extensive rear yard and rear access.\nThe building extends in total to approx.. 230 sqm and boasts a substantial commercial unit on ground floor, and residential accommodation overhead, gated entrance into a secure massive yard to the rear from Green Alley.\nAccommodation comprises: ground floor retail / commercial unit with extensive storage rooms that extends to approx. 170sqm. First floor : two rooms. Second Floor: two rooms + w.c. approx. 60sqm\n\nSuperb Development Opportunity\nExcellent location within walking distance of all amenities and services in Athy Town Centre. \nThe local train station is within walking distance.\nThese derelict properties present a unique opportunity for those with a vision for renovation or redevelopment.\nAthy is a market town located in Southwest County Kildare at the confluence of the River Barrow and the Grand Canal. The town has had a colourful history having developed from a 12th century Anglo-Norman settlement to an important stronghold on the local Estate of the FitzGerald, Earls of Kildare, which gives the town a brilliant sense of character today. \n\nAthy has several schools, restaurants and sports clubs to offer, making it a sought-after location in Kildare. \nLocated between two motorways, the M7 connecting Dublin with Limerick and Cork, and the M9 connecting Dublin with Kilkenny and Waterford. \nThe town is served by a railway station to the east on the Dublin to Waterford intercity route. \n\nAthy is a town continuing to grow with a population currently of 12,000 people but has strong potential to grow beyond 20,000 people. \n\nThe property is zoned 'Town Centre' under the Athy Local Area Plan 2021 2027. \nThe new Local Area Plan will be in place from 2028 onwards.\n\nThe potential purchaser will be required to substantially complete works on this property so as to render it non-derelict and return it to residential use within 24-30 months from the closing of the sale. \nThere will be a buyback option for the council should the works not be completed within the required timeframe.\n\nPlease review the Special Condition on the Contract\nhttps://kildarecoco.ie/AllServices/Housing/RegenerationandVacantHomes/VacantpropertyRefurbishmentGrant/\n\nPlease note special condition clause on contract:\n15. In the event that there has been no development of the subject property, in accordance with the terms of any Planning permission if applicable within a period of 18/24/30 calendar months from the closing date of this Contract or such further period thereafter as the Vendor may allow. The Vendor at its sole discretion shall have an option to request that the subject property be transferred back to the Vendor subject to the Purchaser being refunded the purchase price as per this Contract less 10% being a contribution to the Vendor's costs, i.e. 90% of the purchase price only shall be discharged to the Purchaser without any other interest, costs, or compensation. This clause shall be included in the Deed of Transfer to the Purchaser on closing and shall be registered as a burden on the Title to the property in sale. Once the property has been developed to the satisfaction of the Vendor, the Vendor through their Solicitors shall then execute a discharge of the burden on Title at no further expense to the Purchaser herein.\n\n\nJoint Agent: Darac O'Neill BSc (Hons) Dip Arb Law MRICS, MSCSI, MCIArb\nDirector\nOffice: 00353 45 856 604\nMobile: 087 965 60 63 \nAddress: Trident House, Dublin Road, Naas, Co Kildare\n\nRegister on https://www.mysherryfitz.ie/buyers/sign_in#register to place offers"
      },
